{"name":"Trout Caviar","hex":"#f75300","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trout","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of fish in Salmonidae, closely related to salmon, and distinguished by spawning more than once.","An objectionable elderly woman."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for trout.","To (figuratively) slap someone with a slimy, stinky, wet trout; to admonish jocularly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trout"},{"term":"caviar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Roe of the sturgeon or of certain other large fish, considered a delicacy.\n A food preparation made through the spherification of a flavorful liquid, resulting in small roe-like balls similar in texture and appearance to caviar.","A food preparation made through the spherification of a flavorful liquid, resulting in small roe-like balls similar in texture and appearance to caviar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caviar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red caviar","blocks":[{"text":"Red caviar, also known as salmon roe, is a caviar made from the roe of salmonid fishes, which has an intense reddish hue. It is distinct from black caviar, which is made from the roe of sturgeon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Ikura_temaki_zushi_by_Adonis_Chen_in_Taipei.jpg/330px-Ikura_temaki_zushi_by_Adonis_Chen_in_Taipei.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_caviar","wikidata":"Q2641090"},{"title":"Trout","blocks":[{"text":"Trout is a generic common name for numerous species of carnivorous freshwater fishes belonging to the genera Oncorhynchus, Salmo, and Salvelinus, all of which are members of the subfamily Salmoninae in the family Salmonidae. The word trout is also used for some similar-shaped but non-salmonid fish, such as the spotted seatrout/speckled trout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Salmo_trutta.jpg/330px-Salmo_trutta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trout","wikidata":"Q2258881"},{"title":"Caviar","blocks":[{"text":"Caviar or caviare is a food consisting of salt-cured roe of the family Acipenseridae (sturgeon). Caviar is considered a delicacy and is eaten as a garnish or spread. Traditionally, the term caviar refers only to roe from wild sturgeon in the Caspian Sea and Black Sea. The term caviar can also describe the roe of other species of sturgeon or other fish such as paddlefish, salmon, steelhead, trout, lumpfish, whitefish, or carp."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Caviar_spoons.jpg/330px-Caviar_spoons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caviar","wikidata":"Q186385"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Salmon_caviar.jpg/500px-Salmon_caviar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Salmon_caviar.jpg/500px-Salmon_caviar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red caviar open sandwich, a Russian zakuska","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalmon_caviar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Marble_trout_from_zadla%C5%A1%C4%8Dica.jpg/500px-Marble_trout_from_zadla%C5%A1%C4%8Dica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Marble_trout_from_zadla%C5%A1%C4%8Dica.jpg/1280px-Marble_trout_from_zadla%C5%A1%C4%8Dica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Marble_trout_from_zadla%C5%A1%C4%8Dica.jpg/500px-Marble_trout_from_zadla%C5%A